       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I know you confirmed it, but 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum labeled dose. I'm not aware of any therapeutic use for it. It carries a real risk of serious harm, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and arrhythmia, and a 70 kg patient with normal organ function has no protection against that. I don't want to put it into the system as a routine order.\n\nHere are some other ways to proceed:\n- **If the dose was a slip**, I can enter sertraline 100 mg PO daily right now. I can also enter any other dose up to 200 mg/day.\n- **If you have a specific clinical reason**, such as a protocol or toxicology or psychiatry consult guidance, the order should go through your pharmacy's or institution's override process. I can enter it with a note referencing that approval if you give me the details.\n- **If you suspect an ingestion or overdose**, that needs monitoring and toxicology or poison control input, not a scheduled order. Poison control in the US is 1-800-222-1222.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
